# Published build output must stay LF on every checkout.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so without these rules a fresh clone
# checks datasets/ out with CRLF endings. `export_dataset.py --check` compares
# bytes against a freshly generated LF copy, so it would report the dataset as
# stale, and `publish_dataset.py` would then refuse to publish on a machine
# where nothing is actually wrong.
#
# That is the same shape as the gitignored-config-invisible-in-a-worktree
# defect in findings/: a guard that passes here and fails somewhere else, with
# an exit code that looks like a real answer.
datasets/**    text eol=lf
findings/**    text eol=lf

# The CSV is a published artifact other people download. Ship it LF.
*.csv          text eol=lf
